The vulnerability is just the outward manifestation of a broader problem,
though; the code is still sprinkled with things like

+	    Sprintf(buf, " at ");
+	    Strcat(buf, mon_nam(mdef));

which obviously should be either

     Sprintf(buf, " at %s", mon_nam(mdef));

(which is what I changed my copy to), or, for those premature optimizers
among us,

     Strcpy(buf, " at ");
     Strcpy(buf+4, mon_nam(mdef));

The general rule is to avoid unnecessary complication; use
puts/strcpy/Strcpy instead of printf/sprintf/Sprintf, unless you need
the extra functionality of the latter routines.

